QuickTasks — Version 1.35
Date: 2026-11-25
Status: SHIPPED to GitHub (tag v1.35). Final fix for the iPhone drag-and-drop
        status change: the "scroll back to the top" helper that fires when a card
        is pulled out of Pending is now gated to full-browser only, so a phone
        drag is no longer yanked to the top (the device's own edge auto-scroll
        handles it instead). Code-only; no data change.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
v1.35 changes (vs v1.34):
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  FIX — don't auto-scroll-to-top on a small/touch viewport:
     - When a card is dragged out of Pending, the page auto-scrolls smoothly back
       to the top so the other buckets are visible for the drop. That is a useful
       convenience on a FULL BROWSER (columns stack tall, buckets go off-screen),
       but on an iPhone it fights the device's own edge auto-scroll: the moment
       the card leaves Pending the page jumped to the top, forcing the user to
       scroll back down to find In Progress.
     - The `dragover` watcher that triggers startAutoScrollToTop() now runs only
       when isFullBrowser() is true (window.innerWidth > 900, the wide
       side-by-side layout). Below that the forced scroll-to-top is skipped, so
       the device's native edge auto-scroll does the work.
     - Verified: at 1280px leaving the source column smooth-scrolls to the top;
       at 390px it does not.

  FILES: index.html only (isFullBrowser() gate on the dragover scroll-to-top
  watcher). No api.php / admin.html / css change. Production boards/*.json are
  production-only and are not carried in this repo.

QuickTasks — Version 1.34
Date: 2026-11-21
Status: SHIPPED to GitHub (tag v1.34). Bug fix to the v1.32/v1.33 bonus feature:
        the post-goal prize ladder was LINEAR, so every award cost the same and
        the difficulty never escalated. Code-only; no data change.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
v1.34 changes (vs v1.33):
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  BUG FIX - bonus awards now escalate instead of increasing linearly:
     - The v1.32 default in normPrizes() was threshold = goal + (i + 1): one
       whole extra point per prize, i.e. a strictly LINEAR ladder. Over a goal
       of 10 that put the awards at 11 / 12 / 13, so each prize cost exactly
       the same as the last and the run of prizes was trivially cheap.
     - Replaced with an ESCALATING ladder (BONUS_LADDER = [0.10, 0.30, 0.60]):
       prize i requires goal * (1 + pct) total team points, so each award costs
       10% / 30% / 60% ... of the weekly goal in EXTRA points past the goal.
       The marginal price climbs 1 -> 2 -> 3 points, so the awards get
       progressively harder to earn instead of staying flat.
     - Over a goal of 10: prize 1 = 11.00 (+10%), prize 2 = 13.00 (+30%),
       prize 3 = 16.00 (+60%). "Points to go" stays measured against the points
       already banked (e.g. at 11.08 pts prize 2 reads "1.92 to go", prize 3
       "4.92 to go"), which is the behaviour Michael confirmed he wants.
     - An explicit threshold in config.bonusPrizes still wins; the ladder only
       fills in thresholds that are missing, so boards that hand-set values are
       unaffected. A random per-week "bonus roll" that was prototyped is
       deliberately NOT shipped: a lottery can revoke a prize the kids already
       unlocked, which is unacceptable. No Math.random in the bonus path.
     - Comparison uses the unrounded points value, so thresholds cannot drift
       as the week progresses.

  FILES: index.html only (BONUS_LADDER + bonusSpecThreshold(), and the
  threshold default inside normPrizes()). No api.php / admin.html / css change.
  Production boards/*.json are production-only and are not carried in this repo.

