QuickTasks — Version 1.32
Date: 2026-11-21
Status: SHIPPED to GitHub (tag v1.32). New feature: post-goal BONUS PRIZES on the
        Team Points banner. Code-only feature + a bonusPrizes config sample; the
        prod boards data (prod-only, not carried in repo) is untouched.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
v1.32 changes (vs v1.31):
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  FEATURE — post-goal "bonus prizes" on the Team Points banner:
     - After the team clears the 100% weekly point goal, each whole point of
       OVERAGE (points past the goal) reveals the next prize, in order. A gold,
       gently-pulsing "Bonus - .NN" badge shows the live overage as the headline
       reward number (e.g. "Bonus - 1.15").
     - Prizes render as compact chips UNDER the milestone badges and ABOVE the
       progress meter (inside .points-middle, not a new row), so the team-points
       section NEVER grows in height.
     - Progressive thresholds (per prize, configured): #1 = goal +10%,
       #2 = goal +20%, #3 = goal +30% (each a {text, threshold} object). The
       threshold is the total team-points value at which that prize lights.
       (A random 0..1 extra can be layered per week; this release ships fixed
       +10/20/30% for testability + reproducible data.)
     - Locked (not-yet-earned) prizes show a small dimmed slot: gift icon + a
       lock glyph. The prize NAME is hidden (display:none) so the chip stays
       compact — it reads just [gift] [lock] [N.NN to go]. Only the NEXT pending
       prize shows its "N.NN to go" count (right of the lock); the others show
       just the lock. When earned, the chip pops gold and the name reveals.
     - Config: per-board config.bonusPrizes — an array of strings or
       {text, threshold} objects (or a single string/object). No prizes
       configured -> the whole bonus section is hidden. Sample added to
       boards/children.json:
       [{text:"wday - Nitro",threshold:11.0},
        {text:"wday - Flanigans",threshold:12.0},
        {text:"wday - JapanInn",threshold:13.0}].
     - Reveal is per-prize threshold based (prize i lights when points >=
       threshold[i]), not a fixed "one whole point each", so the progressive
       +10/20/30% bars are honored exactly. The whole section auto-hides when a
       board has no goal or no prizes, and resets with the week's points.
     - Screenshots in docs/screenshots/: TeamPoints_stateA_allDimmed.png
       (goal met, all locked) + TeamPoints_stateB_oneLit.png (first prize lit).

  FILES:
     - index.html — bonus HTML moved into .points-middle (badges row -> bonus
       button -> prize row, above the meter); chip build + per-threshold reveal
       loop; "to go" shown on the next-pending prize only.
     - css/style.css — .points-middle column stack; .points-miles-row;
       .points-bonus-badge (gold pulse); .bonus-chip (compact pill, locked =
       hidden name + lock, lit = gold pop); .bonus-need (next-pending count).
     - boards/children.json — config.bonusPrizes sample (prod data otherwise
       untouched).
     - docs/screenshots/ — the two Team Points state images.
     - No api.php / admin.html change. Fresh-load guard still PASSes (unknown
       config keys merge over DEFAULT_CONFIG; bonusPrizes is not required).

